# Source measurements

Snapshot: `#{s['commit']}`. Physical lines include comments and blank lines. File counts and category totals are in SOURCE_SIZE.csv; per-file hashes and lengths are in SNAPSHOT.json.

- Tracked mathematical source, excluding the root import driver and designated audit/smoke-check modules: **#{core} lines**.
- All tracked Atlas sources including those drivers: **#{c['core_tracked']} lines**.
- Untracked source drafts preserved: **#{c['core_untracked']} lines**.
- All Atlas source files on disk: **#{c['core_all']} lines in #{c['core_files']} files**. This is not a claim that every draft compiles or is imported.
- Pinned mathlib checkout: **#{c['external_sources']['.lake/packages/mathlib']['lines']} physical Lean lines**, including its tests/tools/archive where present; not just mathematical library theorems.

Generated data cannot be reliably separated from ordinary source by provenance in this checkout. “Data”, “Table”, and “generated by” often describe mathematics, not automatic file generation. No invented handwritten total is supplied. Explicit matrices and finite tables remain in the mixed mathematical-source category. Audit/extraction material and external dependencies are separate. The token/provenance searches are discovery aids, not classifications.

## Proof footprints

CODE_COUNTS.csv uses 36 selected compiled roots: one order and one simplicity theorem for each of 18 entries. Each closure traverses constants in types and values (including opaque values, implicit instances, and inductive/recursor metadata). Each recoverable declaration range is assigned to the compiler module of its **range parent**, which can differ from the module of a generated helper. Nested/generated helpers without a range inherit the nearest named parent range. End positions at column zero exclude that final line. Each physical source line is counted once per union.

Ranges include statement, proof/definition body, and interior comments/blank lines. They generally exclude imports and preceding documentation. These are dependency footprints, not just the final wrapper's length. They are not measures of mathematical difficulty, human effort, executable complexity, or complete foundational proof size.

The global deduplicated ATLAS footprint is **#{c['principal_atlas_union']} lines**. The external recoverable footprint is **#{c['principal_external_union']} lines**, a **partial lower measurement**: built-in and generated external declarations may have no recoverable source range. MISSING_RANGES.csv lists every omitted (entry, declaration) pair; #{c['missing_atlas_ranges']} such ATLAS omissions and #{c['missing_external_ranges']} external pairs occur. Counts of pairs are not counts of distinct missing declarations. The graph retains these dependencies even when their source lines are unavailable. Do not add the group rows or the order/simplicity columns: they share most prerequisites.

No generated-data fraction of either footprint is claimed. Source coverage is determined from actual imported-module metadata in Evidence.lean, not guessed from public namespace names. This run retains incremental Lake caching; it is not a fresh measurement of kernel rechecking time and does not time a mathlib rebuild.
