# ATLAS status audit — 14 September 2026

At source `#{s['commit']}`, the compiled catalogue contains **3 completed families and 15 completed sporadic constructions**, each with exact order and simplicity results: **18/18 order entries and 18/18 simplicity entries**, represented by 36 principal declarations. Cyclic prime-order groups are commutative; the other 17 entries have separate noncommutativity results in the selected public interface.

The families are C_p (p prime), A_n (n≥5 for nonabelian simplicity), and PSL_n(F), uniformly for finite fields and n≥2, excluding (n,|F|)=(2,2),(2,3) for simplicity. A_3 is cyclic simple; it is not another family. Type-A prime-power existence is extracted with p prime, f≥1, n≥2 and those two exclusions.

#{table}

All models are actual constructed carriers. Parameters selecting Golay dodecads or distinct coordinates in Mathieu interfaces are geometric choices in existing finite structures, not assumed sporadic order/simplicity certificates. Standard dodecad choices and construction/existence interfaces are extracted. Arbitrary theorem parameters and typeclass hypotheses are retained verbatim in THEOREM_STATEMENTS.txt.

## Checking performed now

- Current pinned default `lake build` passed **5,203 jobs**, covering Atlas and Atlas.Audit. This was an incremental build, with cached messages replayed where applicable, not a from-scratch proof recheck.
- Fresh compiled statement/axiom/graph extraction passed for **#{t['selected']} selected roots**, reaching **#{t['nodes']} declarations**. Graph traversal includes types and proof bodies; no missing graph nodes.
- The exact axiom union is `propext`, `Classical.choice`, `Quot.sound`. No project axiom, sorryAx, or native reduction trust axiom occurs. Name-search hits Classical.axiomOfChoice and Classical.axiom_of_choice are proved classical lemmas, not additional axioms.
- The Atlas source token scan found no sorry, admit, axiom or native_decide tokens. This scan supplements the compiled audit.
- Model-definition and foundations extraction, synthesized concrete group/finite instances, and compiler source-range mapping passed. No ATLAS principal dependency lacks a recoverable parent source range.
- Proof sources and dependency pins were hashed before and after. Existing drafts were preserved. SOURCE_COVERAGE.csv identifies unimported files; no claim is made that all such drafts compile.

## Remaining work and limits

Eleven sporadics have no completed public construction in the inventory: J1, J3, J4, He, Ru, O'N, HN, Ly, Th, B, M. The other classical, exceptional/twisted Lie families and the Tits group remain objectives in this ATLAS catalogue; possible partial mathlib infrastructure is not counted as an ATLAS construction.

Recognition/uniqueness identifying an arbitrary group from a CFSG characterization is not automatically supplied by order and simplicity. Internal full-group comparisons and embeddings are recorded separately. No Moonshine module or VOA comparison is certified by the Fischer construction: its starting point is the explicit Conway–Parker algebra from Golay/Parker data.

This audit does not rerun all historical comparator checks, every separate extension certificate, or a clean mathlib build. It does not verify the Lean kernel implementation, hardware, or the mathematical interpretation independently. Generated-vs-ordinary source provenance is unresolved; external footprint ranges are partial. Those limitations do not turn the checked order/simplicity statements into assumed hypotheses.

CATALOGUE.md has stale J2 and duplicate HS status text; the Mathieu24 base file also has an old comment excluding simplicity although later imported modules provide it. This audit records the actual declarations and leaves those owner files unchanged.

The global selected ATLAS proof footprint is **#{c['principal_atlas_union']} lines**; tracked mathematical source excluding designated drivers/checks is **#{core} lines**. See METRICS.md for exact scope.
